{"repositoryId":21604114,"availability":"available","full":"drostlab/orthologr","name":"orthologr","description":"Genome wide orthology inference and dNdS estimation","category":"Other","language":"R","stars":99,"forks":30,"created":"2014-07-08T08:01:29Z","updated":"2026-10-09T07:40:49Z","license":"GPL-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://drostlab.github.io/orthologr/","topics":["biomartr","blast","blast-searches","codon-alignment","comparative","comparative-genomics","comparative-genomics-studies","comparing-genomes","dnds-estimation","entire-genomes","genomics","genomics-studies","orthologous-genes","orthology-inference","proteome","r","retrieve-genomes","sequence-alignment","sequence-alignments","species"],"demo":"https://drostlab.github.io/orthologr/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.173Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.173Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.173Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.173Z","stars":99,"forks":30}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The comparative method is a powerful approach in genomics research. Based on our knowledge about the phylogenetic relationships between species, we can study the evolution, diversification, and constraints of biological processes by comparing genomes, genes, and other genomic loci across species. The orthologr package aims to provide a framework to perform large scale comparative genomics studies with R. Orthologr aims to be as easy to use as possible - from genomic data retrieval to orthology inference and dNdS estimation between several genomes.","In combination with the R package biomartr, users can retrieve genomes, proteomes, or coding sequences for several species and use them as input for orthology inference and dN/dS estimation with orthologr. The advantage of using biomartr in combination with orthologr is that users can join the new wave of research that promotes and facilitates computational reproducibility in genomics studies and solve the issue of comparing genomes with different genome assembly qualities (also referred to as genome version crisis).","You can find a detailed list of all orthologr functions here:"],"features":["Perform Orthology Inference and dNdS Estimation","Perform Only Orthology Inference","Perform BLAST Searches","Perform Divergence Stratigraphy","Perform Sequence Alignments"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drostlab/orthologr/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"dc7c0af97e9a26825e6766becb16e19f9a2623aec0374a3bd391fd7483458ba5","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.353Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.353Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The comparative method is a powerful approach in genomics research. Based on our knowledge about the phylogenetic relationships between species, we can study the evolution, diversification, and constraints of biological processes by comparing genomes, genes, and other genomic loci across species. The orthologr package aims to provide a framework to perform large scale comparative genomics studies with R. Orthologr aims to be as easy to use as possible - from genomic data retrieval to orthology inference and dNdS estimation between several genomes.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drostlab/orthologr/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"dc7c0af97e9a26825e6766becb16e19f9a2623aec0374a3bd391fd7483458ba5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drostlab/orthologr/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.353Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T07:40:49Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drostlab/orthologr/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.354Z","hash":"dc7c0af97e9a26825e6766becb16e19f9a2623aec0374a3bd391fd7483458ba5","originalBytes":13898,"storedBytes":13898,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["orthologr","perform","install","package","inference","at1g010","dnds","genomes","